stellar-wim (0.8.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fade views out on minimize and when a tab is hidden; the scene node stays
    enabled until the fade finishes.
  * Tab groups accept 2..32 window ids over IPC, can extend existing groups,
    have clickable bar segments and share one geometry across members.
  * Add five tiling modes (master-stack, horizontal, vertical, grid, hybrid),
    configurable master ratio/columns/min-max limits and per-window
    stellarTilingMode rules.
  * Add TILING SET and enrich TILING STATUS with mode/master_ratio/columns.
    The minimal and enhanced profiles now also toggle visual effects.
  * Strip every build-only subproject destination from Meson's install plan
    at install time, instead of removing usr/lib in the Debian rules.
  * Add the Stellar Configuration API: validated, atomic CONFIG GET/LIST/SET/
    RESET/STATUS with live or deferred application and config events.
  * Manage safe argument-free keybindings and validated window-rule properties
    through CONFIG KEYBINDINGS and CONFIG RULES; arbitrary commands are rejected.
  * Preserve CLI argument case so keys, theme names and rule identifiers are
    not corrupted, while verb matching remains case-insensitive.

 -- Stellar WiM Maintainers <stellar-wim@example.invalid>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

stellar-wim (0.7.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Enable animations, drop shadows and opacity by default.
  * Initial Stellar WiM source package (Fase 6).
  * Ships the compositor, stellar-wimctl, session metadata, man pages and
    example configuration under names that do not collide with Labwc.

 -- Stellar WiM Maintainers <stellar-wim@example.invalid>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
